HYPOTHESIS: Summed social capital (ZCU_AU + Zamber + ZMonument) peaked in the 13th century BCE, centred on BCE 1300-1201 (max at BCE 1300, sum=4.24 Z-units), with the adjacent century (BCE 1200/1400) nearly tied (3.62/4.24). Components at the peak:
  Copper&Gold (ZCU_AU) +2.54: above its long-run mean (peak 1100);
  MonumentCount (ZMonument) +1.71: above its long-run mean + rising vs preceding century (its max is BCE 2700);
  Amber (Zamber) -0.01: rising vs preceding century (amber max is BCE 3000).
Interpolated-1yr cross-check confirms 14th c. BCE. Sensitivity all-12 sum peaks BCE 1400 (14th c. BCE), slightly later (late Bronze-Age dagger/depot/house-size surge), but the fixed 3-component social-capital index peaks in the 13th c. BCE.

